{"kind":"article","variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/snapshottesting\/migratingto1.17"]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SnapshotTesting\/documentation\/SnapshotTesting"]]},"abstract":[{"text":"Learn how to use the new ","type":"text"},{"code":"withSnapshotTesting","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" tool for customizing how snapshots are generated and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"diffs displayed.","type":"text"}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/SnapshotTesting\/documentation\/SnapshotTesting\/MigratingTo1.17"},"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"metadata":{"title":"Migrating to 1.17","modules":[{"name":"SnapshotTesting"}],"roleHeading":"Article","role":"article"},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This library is under constant development, and we are always looking for ways to simplify the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"library, and make it more powerful. This version of the library has deprecated some APIs,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"introduced a new APIs, and includes beta support for Swift’s new native testing library."}]},{"level":2,"text":"Customizing snapshots","type":"heading","anchor":"Customizing-snapshots"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Currently there are two global variables in the library for customizing snapshot testing:","type":"text"}]},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SnapshotTesting\/documentation\/SnapshotTesting\/isRecording"},{"type":"text","text":" determines whether new snapshots are generated and saved to disk when the test"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"runs."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SnapshotTesting\/documentation\/SnapshotTesting\/diffTool"},{"type":"text","text":" determines the command line tool that is used to inspect the diff of two files on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"disk."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"These customization options have a few downsides currently.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"First, because they are globals they can easily bleed over from test to test in unexpected ways."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"And further, Swift’s new testing library runs parallel tests in the same process, which is in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"stark contrast to XCTest, which runs parallel tests in separate processes. This means there are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"even more chances for these globals to bleed from one test to another."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"And second, these options aren’t as granular as some of our users wanted. When ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SnapshotTesting\/documentation\/SnapshotTesting\/isRecording","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is true snapshots are generated and written to disk, and when it is false snapshots are not","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"generated, ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"unless"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" a file is not present on disk. The a snapshot ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"is","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" generated. Some of our","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"users wanted an option between these two extremes, where snapshots would not be generated if the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"file does not exist on disk.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"And the "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SnapshotTesting\/documentation\/SnapshotTesting\/diffTool"},{"type":"text","text":" variable allows one to specify a command line tool to use for visualizing"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"diffs of files, but only works when the command line tool accepts a very narrow set of"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"arguments,  _e.g.:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"sh","code":["ksdiff \/path\/to\/file1.png \/path\/to\/file2.png"]}]}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Because of these reasons, the globals "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SnapshotTesting\/documentation\/SnapshotTesting\/isRecording","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SnapshotTesting\/documentation\/SnapshotTesting\/diffTool","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" are now deprecated, and we"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"have introduced a new tool that greatly improves upon all of these problems. There is now a function"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"called "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SnapshotTesting\/documentation\/SnapshotTesting\/withSnapshotTesting(record:diffTool:snapshotNaming:referenceStorage:locale:timeZone:calendar:operation:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"for customizing snapshots. It"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"allows you to customize how the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"assertSnapshot"},{"type":"text","text":" tool behaves for a well-defined scope."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Rather than overriding ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"isRecording"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"diffTool"},{"text":" directly in your tests, you can wrap your test in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"withSnapshotTesting"},{"text":":","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"columns":[{"size":1,"content":[{"code":["\/\/ Before","","func testFeature() {","  isRecording = true ","  diffTool = \"ksdiff\"","  assertSnapshot(…)","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"}]},{"size":1,"content":[{"type":"codeListing","code":["\/\/ After","","func testFeature() {","  withSnapshotTesting(record: .all, diffTool: .ksdiff) {","    assertSnapshot(…)","  }","}"],"syntax":"swift"}]}],"numberOfColumns":2,"type":"row"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If you want to override the options for an entire test class, you can override the "},{"code":"invokeTest","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"method of "},{"code":"XCTestCase","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":":"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"row","numberOfColumns":2,"columns":[{"content":[{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["\/\/ Before","","class FeatureTests: XCTestCase {","  override func invokeTest() {","    isRecording = true ","    diffTool = \"ksdiff\"","    defer { ","      isRecording = false","      diffTool = nil","    }","    super.invokeTest()","  }","}"]}],"size":1},{"content":[{"code":["\/\/ After","","class FeatureTests: XCTestCase {","  override func invokeTest() {","    withSnapshotTesting(record: .all, diffTool: .ksdiff) {","      super.invokeTest()","    }","  }","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"}],"size":1}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"And if you want to override these settings for "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"all"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" tests, then you can implement a base"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"XCTestCase"},{"type":"text","text":" subclass and have your tests inherit from it."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Further, the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"diffTool"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"record"},{"type":"text","text":" arguments have extra customization capabilities:"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"diffTool","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is now a "},{"overridingTitleInlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"function"}],"type":"reference","overridingTitle":"function","identifier":"doc:\/\/SnapshotTesting\/documentation\/SnapshotTesting\/SnapshotTestingConfiguration\/DiffTool-swift.struct","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":""},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"(String, String) -> String","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" that is handed the current snapshot file and the failed snapshot"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"file. It can return the command that one can run to display a diff. For example, to use"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"ImageMagick’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"compare"},{"type":"text","text":" command and open the result in Preview.app:"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["extension SnapshotTestingConfiguration.DiffTool {","  static let compare = Self { ","    \"compare \\\"\\($0)\\\" \\\"\\($1)\\\" png: | open -f -a Preview.app\" ","  }","}"]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"record","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is now a "},{"isActive":true,"overridingTitleInlineContent":[{"text":"type","type":"text"}],"overridingTitle":"type","type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SnapshotTesting\/documentation\/SnapshotTesting\/SnapshotTestingConfiguration\/Record-swift.struct"},{"type":"text","text":" with 4"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"choices: "},{"code":"all","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"missing","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"never","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"failed","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":":"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"all"},{"type":"text","text":": All snapshots will be generated and saved to disk."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"missing"},{"text":": only the snapshots that are missing from the disk will be generated","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and saved.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"never"},{"type":"text","text":": No snapshots will be generated, even if they are missing. This option is appropriate"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"when running tests on CI so that re-tries of tests do not surprisingly pass after snapshots are","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"unexpectedly generated.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"failed","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":": Snapshots only for failing tests will be generated. This can be useful for tests"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that use precision thresholds so that passing tests do not re-record snapshots that are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"subtly different but still within the threshold."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]}]}]},{"anchor":"Beta-support-for-Swift-Testing","level":2,"text":"Beta support for Swift Testing","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This release of the library provides beta support for Swift’s native Testing library. Prior to this"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"release, using "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"assertSnapshot"},{"type":"text","text":" in a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Test"},{"text":" would result in a passing test no matter what. That is","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"because under the hood "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"assertSnapshot"},{"type":"text","text":" uses "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"XCTFail"},{"type":"text","text":" to trigger test failures, but that does not"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"cause test failures when using Swift Testing."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In version 1.17 the "},{"code":"assertSnapshot","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" helper will now intelligently figure out if tests are running"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"in an XCTest context or a Swift Testing context, and will determine if it should invoke "},{"code":"XCTFail","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"Issue.record","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" to trigger a test failure."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"For the most part you can write tests for Swift Testing exactly as you would for XCTest. However,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"there is one major difference. In order to override a snapshot’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SnapshotTesting\/documentation\/SnapshotTesting\/SnapshotTestingConfiguration","overridingTitle":"configuration","overridingTitleInlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"configuration"}],"type":"reference"},{"text":" for a particular test or an entire suite you","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"must use what are known as “test traits”:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["import SnapshotTesting","","@Suite(.snapshots(record: .all, diffTool: .ksdiff))","struct FeatureTests {","  …","}"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"That will override the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"diffTool"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"record"},{"type":"text","text":" options for the entire "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FeatureTests"},{"type":"text","text":" suite."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"These traits can also be used on individual "},{"code":"@Test","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"s too.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"references":{"doc://SnapshotTesting/documentation/SnapshotTesting/SnapshotTestingConfiguration/DiffTool-swift.struct":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Describes the diff command used to diff two files on disk."}],"url":"\/documentation\/snapshottesting\/snapshottestingconfiguration\/difftool-swift.struct","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"DiffTool","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"DiffTool"}],"title":"SnapshotTestingConfiguration.DiffTool","identifier":"doc:\/\/SnapshotTesting\/documentation\/SnapshotTesting\/SnapshotTestingConfiguration\/DiffTool-swift.struct","kind":"symbol","type":"topic"},"doc://SnapshotTesting/documentation/SnapshotTesting":{"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/snapshottesting","title":"SnapshotTesting","type":"topic","role":"collection","abstract":[{"text":"Powerfully flexible snapshot testing.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SnapshotTesting\/documentation\/SnapshotTesting"},"doc://SnapshotTesting/documentation/SnapshotTesting/SnapshotTestingConfiguration/Record-swift.struct":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"The record mode of the snapshot test.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Record"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SnapshotTesting\/documentation\/SnapshotTesting\/SnapshotTestingConfiguration\/Record-swift.struct","title":"SnapshotTestingConfiguration.Record","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Record","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/snapshottesting\/snapshottestingconfiguration\/record-swift.struct"},"doc://SnapshotTesting/documentation/SnapshotTesting/SnapshotTestingConfiguration":{"title":"SnapshotTestingConfiguration","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/SnapshotTesting\/documentation\/SnapshotTesting\/SnapshotTestingConfiguration","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/snapshottesting\/snapshottestingconfiguration","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The configuration for a snapshot test."}],"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"SnapshotTestingConfiguration","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"SnapshotTestingConfiguration"}]},"doc://SnapshotTesting/documentation/SnapshotTesting/diffTool":{"role":"symbol","deprecated":true,"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","title":"diffTool","url":"\/documentation\/snapshottesting\/difftool","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Enhances failure messages with a command line diff tool expression that can be copied and pasted"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"into a terminal."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SnapshotTesting\/documentation\/SnapshotTesting\/diffTool","fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"diffTool","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:15SnapshotTesting0aB13ConfigurationV","text":"SnapshotTestingConfiguration","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:15SnapshotTesting0aB13ConfigurationV8DiffToolV","text":"DiffTool","kind":"typeIdentifier"}]},"doc://SnapshotTesting/documentation/SnapshotTesting/withSnapshotTesting(record:diffTool:snapshotNaming:referenceStorage:locale:timeZone:calendar:operation:)":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SnapshotTesting\/documentation\/SnapshotTesting\/withSnapshotTesting(record:diffTool:snapshotNaming:referenceStorage:locale:timeZone:calendar:operation:)","kind":"symbol","title":"withSnapshotTesting(record:diffTool:snapshotNaming:referenceStorage:locale:timeZone:calendar:operation:)","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/snapshottesting\/withsnapshottesting(record:difftool:snapshotnaming:referencestorage:locale:timezone:calendar:operation:)","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"withSnapshotTesting"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"R","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">(","kind":"text"},{"text":"record","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SnapshotTestingConfiguration","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:15SnapshotTesting0aB13ConfigurationV"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Record","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:15SnapshotTesting0aB13ConfigurationV6RecordV"},{"text":"?, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"diffTool","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SnapshotTestingConfiguration","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:15SnapshotTesting0aB13ConfigurationV"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"DiffTool","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:15SnapshotTesting0aB13ConfigurationV8DiffToolV"},{"text":"?, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"snapshotNaming","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SnapshotTestingConfiguration","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:15SnapshotTesting0aB13ConfigurationV"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"SnapshotNaming","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:15SnapshotTesting0aB13ConfigurationV0A6NamingO"},{"text":"?, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"referenceStorage","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SnapshotTestingConfiguration","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:15SnapshotTesting0aB13ConfigurationV"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"ReferenceStorage","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:15SnapshotTesting0aB13ConfigurationV16ReferenceStorageO"},{"text":"?, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"locale","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Locale","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:10Foundation6LocaleV"},{"text":"?, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"timeZone","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"TimeZone","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:10Foundation8TimeZoneV"},{"text":"?, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"calendar","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Calendar","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:10Foundation8CalendarV"},{"text":"?, ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"operation"},{"kind":"text","text":": () "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"throws"},{"kind":"text","text":" -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"R"},{"kind":"text","text":") "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"rethrows"},{"kind":"text","text":" -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"R"}],"role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Customizes "},{"code":"assertSnapshot","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" for the duration of an operation."}]},"doc://SnapshotTesting/documentation/SnapshotTesting/isRecording":{"abstract":[{"text":"Whether or not to record all new references.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/snapshottesting\/isrecording","identifier":"doc:\/\/SnapshotTesting\/documentation\/SnapshotTesting\/isRecording","title":"isRecording","role":"symbol","deprecated":true,"fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"isRecording","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Bool","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol"}}}